    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A documented supply-demand imbalance in May 2026, stemming from seasonal heat and other long-running plant outages, set the stage for the grid incident. The trip of Kepco SPC Power's Unit 2 acted as the precipitating event. This cascade of causes—a verified equipment failure compounding pre-existing shortfalls—underscores the importance of distinguishing root causes from immediate triggers in grid stability analysis.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "why-1",
          "why-2",
          "how-0"
        ],
        "center": "why-0",
        "center_kind": "why",
        "channel": "toned",
        "channel_role": "element_centered",
        "composition_mode": "ADR-0008",
        "salience_rank": 1
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "When the tripped unit initiated the sequence, crisis decision-makers ordered a calculated grid protection measure: emergency load shedding. This action, designed to prevent overloading of a critical 230-kilovolt line, represents a standard grid stabilization procedure. The measured response, while resulting in forced demand reduction, was a necessary intervention to preserve overall system integrity following the power outage.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Sage",
